 - 2026-06-23: PHASE A6 (ARC NORTH STAR; operator MANDATORY; INTEGRATION + HEADLINE METRIC) -- consolidate whatever RAISED a real metric (A1 graded goal-energy -> live solve-rate/first-win; A2 expansion prior -> deeper live solve; A3 new bank) into the SUBMITTED_AGENT_CONFIG + the refreshed package; re-measure end-to-end on live solve-rate + live_multi_level_solve_rate + action efficiency + offline_to_live_transfer_ratio + live-submittable count (vs 33). If NONE raised a clean control-passed metric (each gated by its positive control + uniform-energy ablation), keep the bare config + honest null. Avoid the .427 solve-rate TAUTOLOGY (a bare==integrated equality is a null, not a fabrication). Keep test_arc_submitted_agent_parity.py + arc_orphan_solver_lint green. verifier_is_oracle: false. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=success: integrated_live_submittable_raised_config_shipped; results/experiment_4645_integration_gate.json
 - 2026-06-23: PHASE B1 (RESERVED INFRA; co-headline metric) -- add a canonical live_multi_level_solve_rate metric helper: the fraction of live attempts that solve >=2 levels (the NEW WALL -- .427 reached first-win 0.59 but multi-level solve-rate is 0.04), reported SIDE-BY-SIDE with reproducible_total_levels, live-submittable count, first-win-rate, live_action_efficiency, and offline_to_live_transfer_ratio. This is the metric that distinguishes "reached the first level-up" from "solved multiple levels live" -- the gap A1/A2 must close. Asserting tests. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=success: live_multi_level_solve_rate_metric_helper_shipped_tests_green; results/experiment_4646_live_multi_level_solve_rate_metric.json
